---
/**
 * CmsExplainer.astro — Streamlined, high-readability explainer on CMS detection,
 * digital footprints, architecture variations, and non-invasive public inspection.
 * Compact bento layout with high contrast, crisp typography, and balanced proportions.
 */
---

<section class="cms-explainer-section" id="what-is-a-cms-detector" aria-labelledby="explainer-h2">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow-lockup">
        <h2 id="explainer-h2" class="section-title">
          What Is a CMS Detector?
        </h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">
          A plain-English guide to content management systems, digital footprints, and how automated tools identify website platforms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="explainer-grid">
      <!-- Card 1: What is a CMS -->
      <article class="explainer-card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon-wrap icon-wrap--blue" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
              <line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"></line>
              <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"></line>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="card-tag">Architecture & Adoption</span>
        </div>

        <h3 class="explainer-heading">
          What Is a Content Management System (CMS)?
        </h3>

        <p class="explainer-lead">
          A <strong>Content Management System (CMS)</strong> is software that allows teams to create, edit, organize, and publish web content via visual interfaces—without coding HTML or backend scripts for every update.
        </p>

        <div class="architecture-split">
          <div class="arch-block">
            <div class="arch-block-head">
              <span class="arch-title text-white">Open-Source</span>
              <span class="arch-badge">Self-Hosted</span>
            </div>
            <p class="arch-desc">Custom hosting, database autonomy & code access.</p>
            <div class="arch-tags">
              <span class="tech-pill">WordPress</span>
              <span class="tech-pill">Drupal</span>
              <span class="tech-pill">Joomla</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="arch-block">
            <div class="arch-block-head">
              <span class="arch-title text-white">Hosted Builders</span>
              <span class="arch-badge">SaaS Cloud</span>
            </div>
            <p class="arch-desc">Managed edge CDN, drag-and-drop & zero setup.</p>
            <div class="arch-tags">
              <span class="tech-pill">Shopify</span>
              <span class="tech-pill">Webflow</span>
              <span class="tech-pill">Squarespace</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-callout">
          <div class="stat-number">>68%</div>
          <p class="stat-text">
            of all websites run on an identifiable CMS platform according to independent data from <a href="https://w3techs.com/technologies/overview/content_management" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link-soft">W3Techs CMS usage statistics</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 2: How detection works -->
      <article class="explainer-card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon-wrap icon-wrap--brand" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
              <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
              <path d="M11 8v6"></path>
              <path d="M8 11h6"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="card-tag">Signal Harvesting</span>
        </div>

        <h3 class="explainer-heading">
          How a CMS Detector Finds Platform Clues
        </h3>

        <p class="explainer-lead">
          When delivering pages, web servers transmit observable footprints. An automated CMS detector parses these deterministic technical signals:
        </p>

        <div class="signal-inspector">
          <div class="signal-row">
            <div class="signal-meta">
              <span class="signal-badge">Head Tag</span>
              <span class="signal-title text-white">HTML Meta Generator</span>
            </div>
            <div class="code-pill">
              <code>&lt;meta name="generator" content="WordPress"&gt;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="signal-note">
              Self-declared platform metadata embedded in the document <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="signal-row">
            <div class="signal-meta">
              <span class="signal-badge">File Path</span>
              <span class="signal-title text-white">Asset Directory Structures</span>
            </div>
            <div class="code-pill">
              <code>/wp-content/themes/</code> <span class="code-divider">·</span> <code>/sites/default/files/</code>
            </div>
            <p class="signal-note">
              Predictable folder hierarchies for stylesheets, themes, and plugins.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="signal-row">
            <div class="signal-meta">
              <span class="signal-badge">CDN Host</span>
              <span class="signal-title text-white">Hosted Script Hostnames</span>
            </div>
            <div class="code-pill">
              <code>cdn.shopify.com</code> <span class="code-divider">·</span> <code>static.parastorage.com</code>
            </div>
            <p class="signal-note">
              Dedicated cloud endpoints tied directly to managed platforms like Shopify and Wix.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="signal-row">
            <div class="signal-meta">
              <span class="signal-badge">Header</span>
              <span class="signal-title text-white">HTTP Response Headers</span>
            </div>
            <div class="code-pill">
              <code>x-generator: Drupal</code> <span class="code-divider">·</span> <code>x-powered-by</code>
            </div>
            <p class="signal-note">
              Server-level response headers cataloged on <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link-soft">MDN Web Docs</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 3: Why some sites cannot be identified -->
      <article class="explainer-card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon-wrap icon-wrap--purple" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polygon points="12 2 2 7 12 12 22 7 12 2"></polygon>
              <polyline points="2 17 12 22 22 17"></polyline>
              <polyline points="2 12 12 17 22 12"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="card-tag">Detection Limits</span>
        </div>

        <h3 class="explainer-heading">
          Why Some Websites Cannot Be Identified
        </h3>

        <p class="explainer-lead">
          No detector can identify 100% of websites. A result of <em>"No known platform detected"</em> usually stems from modern architecture:
        </p>

        <div class="limit-items">
          <div class="limit-item">
            <div class="limit-item-header">
              <span class="limit-tag">Decoupled</span>
              <h4 class="limit-heading text-white">Headless & Jamstack Architectures</h4>
            </div>
            <p class="limit-text">
              A headless CMS (Sanity, Strapi, Contentful) manages data behind private APIs, while an SSG/SSR framework renders HTML, keeping the CMS invisible.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="limit-item">
            <div class="limit-item-header">
              <span class="limit-tag">Proprietary</span>
              <h4 class="limit-heading text-white">Custom-Built Enterprise Backends</h4>
            </div>
            <p class="limit-text">
              Bespoke internal engines written in Python (Django), Ruby on Rails, Go, or Java that share no common commercial signatures or asset conventions.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="limit-item">
            <div class="limit-item-header">
              <span class="limit-tag">Hardened</span>
              <h4 class="limit-heading text-white">Active Security Hardening</h4>
            </div>
            <p class="limit-text">
              Site administrators often install security modules or proxies that strip <code>&lt;meta name="generator"&gt;</code> tags and obfuscate asset paths.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 4: Safe, Public, Non-Invasive -->
      <article class="explainer-card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon-wrap icon-wrap--green" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
              <polyline points="9 12 11 14 15 10"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="card-tag">Ethics & Compliance</span>
        </div>

        <h3 class="explainer-heading">
          Safe, Public, Non-Invasive Inspection
        </h3>

        <p class="explainer-lead">
          Using our CMS detector is completely safe, legal, and non-invasive. The engine operates strictly identically to an everyday web browser:
        </p>

        <div class="safety-pillars">
          <div class="safety-pillar">
            <div class="safety-check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
                <path d="M13.5 4.5l-7 7L3 8" stroke="var(--color-success)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="safety-content">
              <h4 class="safety-title text-white">100% Passive Read-Only Request</h4>
              <p class="safety-desc">
                Only inspects public HTTP responses and HTML markup deliberately broadcast to every regular visitor.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="safety-pillar">
            <div class="safety-check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
                <path d="M13.5 4.5l-7 7L3 8" stroke="var(--color-success)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="safety-content">
              <h4 class="safety-title text-white">Zero Exploitation or Penetration</h4>
              <p class="safety-desc">
                Never bypasses authentication walls, probes private admin endpoints, or exploits vulnerabilities.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="safety-pillar">
            <div class="safety-check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
                <path d="M13.5 4.5l-7 7L3 8" stroke="var(--color-success)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="safety-content">
              <h4 class="safety-title text-white">Ethical Developer Utility</h4>
              <p class="safety-desc">
                Built for developers, designers, and site owners to audit tech stacks and research web trends.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="trust-ribbon">
          <span class="trust-dot"></span>
          <span class="trust-text">Standard HTTP/2 GET Request · No Credentials Required · Strictly Read-Only</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cms-explainer-section {
    padding-block: clamp(36px, 4vw, 54px);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-soft);
    position: relative;
  }

  .section-header {
    margin-block-end: clamp(18px, 2.5vw, 24px);
  }

  .section-title {
    color: var(--color-on-primary);
    margin-block: 0 6px;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .section-subtitle {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 720px;
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 15.5px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #cbd5e1;
  }

  /* Compact 2x2 Bento Grid */
  .explainer-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .explainer-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: 18px;
    }
  }

  /* Card Styling */
  .explainer-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.75) 0%, rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.9) 100%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-marketing);
    transition: border-color 0.25s ease, transform 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease;
    position: relative;
  }

  .explainer-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 24px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
  }

  .card-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-block-end: 10px;
  }

  .icon-wrap {
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-app-sm);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

